 answer='<strong>TikTok gives a strike for each violation, counted per policy area, and strikes expire after 90 days.</strong> Reaching the strike limit in one area, or across the account, leads to a permanent ban. Severe violations, such as content that endangers children or promotes violence, can lead to a ban on the first strike. You can see violations in the app and appeal each one.',
